# A by-NAME list leaves a new selftest un-ignored by default, so its binary
# can be committed as a tracked ELF; every one of these is built with -g, so
# its DWARF carries the builder's absolute path. The glob makes the default safe; the negation
# keeps the sources, which share the prefix.
capture_cell_at/test_*
!capture_cell_at/test_*.c
capture_cell_diag/kismet_cap_cell_diag
capture_cell_diag/celldiag_probe
# Cross-compiled aarch64 build of the probe (build_celldiag_probe_aarch64.sh) —
# a build artifact for remote PCIe/MHI deploy, not a committed binary.
capture_cell_diag/celldiag_probe-aarch64
capture_cell_diag/diag_logstream_dump
# macOS debug symbols, emitted beside the binary above by `make -f standalone.mk`
# on a darwin host, which the framework-free standalone build exists for.
# Same artifact, different suffix; without this it shows up as an untracked
# directory.
capture_cell_diag/diag_logstream_dump.dSYM/
# Same rule as capture_cell_at/ above: "selftest binaries are build output",
# not "these particular files are build output", so a new selftest is ignored
# by default.  Every tracked `capture_cell_diag/test_*` is a `.c`, so the
# negation loses nothing.
capture_cell_diag/test_*
!capture_cell_diag/test_*.c
capture_sniffle_ble/kismet_cap_sniffle_ble
capture_lorapipe/kismet_cap_lorapipe
kismet_cap_pcapfile
kismet_cap_kismetdb

