# celltools/Makefile is HAND-WRITTEN, not generated by ./configure, so the
# blanket `Makefile` rule above must not swallow it. Same exemption idiom as
# `!packaging/centos/el7/Makefile`. Being hand-written is the point: the checks
# it runs compile nothing and must work on a clone nobody has configured.
!celltools/Makefile

